if you've been following cyberpunk 2077  you probably know how deadly mega  corporations like militech and arasaka  can be  not only can corporate conflicts be  waged economically but many regimes are  enforced through violence  theft and arson some of these conflicts  play out in smaller arenas a gunfight in  the streets of night city or an  assassination attempt on upper  management  however if there's enough resources at  play these contained conflicts can  expand  into full-blown multi-court battles this  is what we call  a corporate war although there were  three corporate wars prior to the fourth  obviously the fourth corporate war  played a big part in shaping the  corporate cultural and environmental  landscape of cyberpunk's universe  even though the war ended 50 years  before the events of cyberpunk 2077  remnants of the war are and always will  be present in night city  but before we dig into the fourth  corporate war let's take a look back at  the previous corporate wars  from 2004 to 2016 corporations were  involved in three distinct wars  most of these conflicts were fought by  security personnel and mercenaries with  high-tech weaponry  the first war was between epic games and  apple  i mean ebm and orbital air for control  over the remains of the failing company  transworld airlines ultimately orbital  air forced ebm to surrender and they  took control of transworld airlines  assets  although this war only lasted from 2004  to 2006 it set a dangerous precedent for  other corporations it meant that  violence and warfare were viable tactics  many corporations beefed up their  security departments when the dust  settled i say when the dust settled but  the dust from corporate warfare didn't  have much time to settle  in 2006 the second corporate war kicked  off  this time the major players were two  massive oil companies petrochem and  sovoil  oil companies engaged in deceit  clandestine warfare and underhanded  tactics  that's the first time i've heard of  something like that while petrochem did  significant damage to silve oil it  ultimately lost the battle with sovoil  coming out on top but the war wreaked  havoc on the world  most notably the southern pacific rim  became a cesspool of pollution and oil  according to cyberpunk 2020 firestorm  stormfront try saying that five times  fast the south china sea became a  lifeless chemical stew all but  inhabitable today  nations and economies were destroyed in  the fallout and so voyle was forced to  pay reparations the second corporate war  was also the first time a corporation  blatantly ignored governments and  nations in order to secure a victory  the third corporate war played out a  little differently than the last two due  to the fact that it was mostly fought on  the net  this war was between investment  councillors meryl asukaga and finch and  the rothstein fund a subsidiary of the  bank of new york  manf was embezzling money from the  rothstein fund when the rothstein fund  uncovered  manf's scheme they notified the los  angeles district attorney's office  manf retaliated by launching a netrunner  assault on the rothstein fund  a few months later manf left the corpses  of two rothstein execs  on the da's doorsteps the rostine fund  dissolved shortly after  the worst was yet to come for night city  in 2021 a german nautical tech company  by the name of  in inter international  handles marine act  or ihag for short came into some  financial trouble two competing nautical  companies caught wind of ihack's  financial downturn  and both attempted to swoop in and take  control of the sinking  pun intended nautical corp those  companies were ocean technology and  energy corporation  otech for short and a french company i'm  not going to try to pronounce  which we'll call sino for short i hag  otech and ceno had been ruthless  competitors for years  vying for economic dominance in marine  biotechnology when ihack filed for  bankruptcy otec encino opened bids to  acquire the company  unfortunately before a ceno negotiator  could present a buyout offered to ihag  she was kidnapped i wonder who or what  could have been behind that  wasting no time at all otech signed a  protection security contract with  militech a huge tech and weapons  corporation that had been in competition  with arasaka for years  of course this caused ceno to partner up  with arasaka the japanese-based  mega-corporation  this more or less kicked off a proxy war  between militech and arasaka officially  both corps are trying to sway the  outcome of the ihag  takeover unofficially the two major  corporations found a reason to launch a  clandestine conflict known as the shadow  war  most of the attacks during this period  consisted of assassination theft and net  raids between arasaka and militech  the shadow raids didn't last long though  as the covert operations of both  companies came to a head  war broke loose known as the hot war  many corpse and security specialists  picked aside and fighting broke out in  all major cities worldwide  at this point the dispute between ceno  and otech had been resolved but the two  massive security corps were just getting  started this squabble was shaping up to  be much bigger than the corporate wars  before it both sides were escalating the  conflict every chance they got  investing heavily in weapons technology  very few parts of the world were off  limits and entire economies societies  and cultures suffered because of it most  notably in 2023  international trade collapsed the net  also suffered from the conflict  it was rife with deadly programs and  dark areas thanks to militech and  arasaka's handiwork netwatch the  internet police couldn't contain the  virtual damage either  eventually the pre-fourth corporate war  net deteriorated  and died 2023 was also the same year  that johnny silverhand and solo morgan  blackhand along with a group of  anarchists  raided the arasaka building and night  city to destroy arasaka's secured  database  for more info on this pivotal event in  johnny's life be sure to check out our  video on johnny silverhand  right after this this raid didn't quite  go as planned and a nuclear device was  set off destroying central night city  and killing three quarters of a million  people it's unclear who detonated the  nuke some believe it was arasaka to  protect corporate secrets  while others believe it to be militech  finally the united states government  stepped in and nationalized militech  forcing arasaka out of the united states  with militech at her back u.s president  elizabeth cress used this as an  opportunity to take full control of the  government and reunify the united states  of course the free state of northern  california was uninterested in  reunification due to northern  california's disobedience crest did not  aid night city and its reconstruction  efforts  and this brings us to the time of the  red but we'll save that for another  video  the fourth corporate war was a wake up  call for the world although governments  and nations still  existed it became apparent that  corporations were calling the shots  allegiances didn't lie in world leaders  or countries but in arasaka or militech  and of course  i'm sure we'll see more of this bitter  rivalry between militech and arasaka in  cyberpunk 2077.  thank you so much for watching this  episode of cyberpunk lore  be sure to check back every saturday for  a new episode and if there's something  you'd like us to discuss  leave it in the comments below or you  can drop me a line on twitter  see you next time  you
 

